# Dynamic export list for binaries that embed the static CPython (ELF linkers:
# GNU ld, LLD). Consumed as `-Wl,--dynamic-list=<this file>`.
#
# Native wheels resolve the CPython C-API from the host executable at dlopen,
# so those symbols must reach the dynamic symbol table. The blanket
# `--export-dynamic` this replaces put EVERY global there instead: 1,292,605
# symbols and 275 MiB of `.dynstr` in a debug `omp`, 23% of the binary, almost
# all of it Rust monomorphizations no extension can name.
#
# The three patterns below are the measured surface, not a guess. Across the
# nine extension modules CPython itself ships in `lib-dynload`, 1018 distinct
# undefined symbols resolve as: 804 matching these patterns, 67 Tcl/Tk (bound
# through DT_NEEDED on libtcl9.0.so, never the host), and the remainder libc,
# libm, and loader stubs. Nothing outside these patterns is sought from the
# executable.
{
	Py*;
	_Py*;
	PY_*;
};
